AB  - The proceedings contain 14 papers. The topics discussed include: geography according to ChatGPT – how generative AI represents and reasons about geography; conceptual neighborhood graphs: event detectors, data relevancy, and language translation; towards GeoAI foundation models: a multimodal learning framework with geospatial intelligence; identifying origins of place names via retrieval augmented generation; simulating parking choices using large language models: experiments with GPT-4o Mini; evaluating the feasibility of ChatGPT for mapping building attributes; how does GPT perceive city similarity?; geospatial mechanistic interpretability of large language models; trust in foundation models and GenAI: a geographic perspective; and geographic bias and diversity in AI evaluation.
