AB  - As a topical issue, Geospatial Artificial Intelligence (GeoAI), allowing geospatial data to be used as an entry point for the most innovative Artificial Intelligence (AI) models, overlaps with another very interesting application topic, namely sustainability. As a measure of the ecosystem's ability to meet current and future needs, this concept uses advanced AI techniques to quantify it, hence the particular interest of GeoAI, while using geospatial data with high application value. This study therefore explores the intersection between GeoAI and sustainability in relation to two main areas of application, especially culture and society on the one hand, and energy and mining on the other. The aim of this work is to provide readers with a comprehensive view of this synergy, while offering them a detailed presentation of the most consistent research in this field. The general question is presented, followed by an illustration of the survey methodology. Next, aspects of the synergy between GeoAI and sustainability are explored in depth, focusing on the two areas of application mentioned above. The challenges facing this combination are also identified, with a concise response to the challenges and questions concerned, supported by metrics and illustrative figures, while discussing the prospects for the future. © 2026 IEEE.
