AB  - GALA, a multi-agent GeoAI framework for mineral exploration. GALA integrates the Segment Anything Model 3 (SAM3)[1] for visual feature extraction, geological knowledge graphs enhanced by GraphRAG[2] for structured reasoning, and a team of collaborative LLM-based agents[3] for expert-like analysis. The model introduces a human-in-the-loop mechanism in which uncertainty triggers expert review, thereby creating a continuous feedback loop that refines both visual outputs and domain knowledge. In preliminary experiments on aerial and GF-2 imagery, GALA improved a mean segmentation F1-score from 0.1606 to 0.6388 for geological features using SAM3-based open-vocabulary segmentation. The framework delivers end-to-end inference on Ascend 910B2 hardware. By integrating multi-modal data, symbolic knowledge, and human expertise into a comprehensible pipeline, GALA enhances transparent and adaptable GeoAI for geoscience decision support, contributing to pivotal domains such as multi-modal GeoAI, geographic knowledge graphs, and human-AI collaboration.  © 2026 IEEE.
