AB  - The proceedings contain 187 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Information Systems and Technologies. The topics include: Performance Evaluation of Oracle APEX Reporting Regions: Page Rendering and Loading Optimization; innovative Culture in the 21st Century: A Bibliometric Study of WoS; loyalty and Brand Experience: A Theoretical Review of Its Evolution and a Literature Review; layer-Sensitive Selective Merge in Multi-source Bibliographic Graphs; DEDL—An Information Model-Based Data Ecosystem Description Language; The Power of GeoSpatial Data Mining and Geo-AI: A Comprehensive Review and Concise Guide for New Developers; advancing Customer Journeys Through the Identification of the Next Best Channel in Digital Marketing; towards a Language Identification Approach for the Detection of Abusive Messages in Tweets of Mixed Wolof-French Codes; assessment of the Effectiveness of Privacy and Data Protection Awareness Training: An Experimental Study; Augmenting Knowledge Graph-Based Decision Support Systems for SMEs by User Collaboration; reducing Bias in Link Prediction; Machine Unlearning for the XGBoost Model with Network Intrusion Datasets; When Avoidance Helps: How Approach and Avoidance Job Crafting Shape Perceived Benefits of AI at Work; Activity-Based Costing (ABC) and Time-Driven ABC (TDABC) in the Maritime and Port Sector: An Integrative Systematic Review; CODE.Clinic: A Framework to Promote Health Data Quality and Best Practices for Hospital Clinical Coding; conceptual Normalisation as a Foundation for Clear and Correct Organisational Models; Comparing Kernel Density Estimation and DBSCAN for Central Region Detection in Urban Last-Mile Delivery; The Battle for Supply Chain Leadership: Analysing the Synergy and Conflict Between the Chief Technology Officer (CTO) and the Chief Operating Officer (COO); when Security Meets Ethics: Balancing Control, Privacy, and Trust in Digital Systems.
