TI  - GeoAI-Driven Spatio-Temporal Super-Resolution for Automated Residential Renewal Priority Detection
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of the 2026 13th International Conference on Computing for Sustainable Global Development, INDIACom 2026
DO  - 10.23919/INDIACom70271.2026.11526419
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105041787691?origin=resultslist
AD  - St. Joseph's College of Engineering, Chennai, India
AB  - The evaluation of urban renewal in old residential areas is of importance to a sustainable and fair urban development. The conventional methods of evaluation require manual survey, subjective scoring, and coarse-resolution information which results to an inconsistent identification of degraded regions. In this research, the automated GeoAI system, which combines high-resolution remote sensors images and deep learning, is suggested as a practical model to perform precise testing of renewal-priority areas. In order to extract finer-scale structural information and detect more reliable features associated with land-use intensity, building aging, and space compactness, satellite images are upsampled with input of ESRGAN-based super-resolution enhancement. Deep Belief Network-Long Short-Term Memory hybrid (DBN-LSTM) model can detect the changes in space and time and classify deteriorated areas. Experimental analysis within a city dwelling setting proves to be much more accurate, doing better than what machine learning on its own can do. The proposed system presents an informative, intelligent decision-support instrument, which can support the role of a planner to decide on the suitability of interventions, resource, and available resource management, and sustainable urban revitalization measures. © 2026 Bharati Vidyapeeth's Institute of Computer Applications and Management (BVICAM).
