AB  - Geospatial data is inherently tied to its precise geographical coordinates on Earth. Various sources of geospatial data, including remote sensing, light detection and range (LiDAR), and the Global Positioning System (GPS), provide varying levels of resolution and distinctive characteristics, making it possible to obtain it from a wide range of sources. Spatial data analysis involves understanding, interpreting, and extracting meaningful insights from geospatial information. Industries and governments use this analysis to improve corporate operations and track resources in infrastructure projects. Artificial Intelligence techniques such as machines and deep learning models have revolutionized this field by providing advanced tools and algorithms to analyze complex spatial datasets. This survey explores various Artificial Intelligence (AI) applications in spatial data analysis. It showcases how these technologies are employed to tackle challenges such as spatial clustering, remote sensing, and satellite imagery analysis. This survey also aims to provide an overview of key concepts in the evolving and interdisciplinary field of geoAI, such as spatial data analysis, machine learning, and deep learning, and present the recent applications of AI algorithms used to analyze geospatial data.  © 2026 IEEE.
