AB  - Integration of geographic artificial intelligence (AI) into irrigation management systems provides a transformative approach to improving the efficiency and sustainability of water use in the agricultural sector. It investigates a comprehensive approach to utilizing Geo-AI technologies, such as AI, to enable data-driven irrigation decisions. Advanced data collection methods, processing, analysis, and machine learning tools are used to predict irrigation needs. This approach integrates various data sources to provide a comprehensive understanding of irrigation requirements. Geo-AI's implementation in irrigation management results in substantial advantages, such as enhanced crop yields, cost reductions, environmental sustainability, and optimized water consumption. This investigation delineates elaborate implementation procedures, including system deployment, continuous optimization, and assessment and planning. Farmers can achieve sustainable farming practices, increased agricultural productivity, and efficient water management by incorporating Geo-AI technologies that are adaptable to a variety of commodities and conditions. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved..
