AB  - Spatial thinking is defined as having the knowledge and skills necessary to employ concepts of space (e.g., physical location) and/or tools of representation (e.g., maps) to solve problems. As such, it involves both cognitive processes and geographic information. The first focuses on how humans perceive and navigate in the physical world, and the second involves analyzing patterns of data that can be digitally mapped. These cognitive skills and geospatial tools can help entrepreneurs leverage many benefits of the digitization of data for better decision-making. © Editors and Contributors Severally 2025 All rights reserved.
