AB  - The use of spatially aware artificial intelligence in studying and monitoring Sustainable Development Goals is examined in this chapter. Spatially aware AI incorporates spatial data and AI algorithms to achieve particular SDGs, such as poverty eradication, hunger eradication, excellent health and wellbeing, quality education, clean water and sanitation, sustainable cities, climate action, life below the water, life on land, and partnerships. The incorporation of GeoAI presents ethical, legal, technical, and social challenges even while it provides useful insights. Collaboration, transparency, accountability, and addressing biases and discrimination are essential to ensure responsible and effective deployment. By overcoming these challenges, stakeholders can accelerate progress toward achieving the SDGs. © 2023 by IGI Global. All rights reserved.
