AB  - Training semantic segmentation models on geospatial data presents challenges due to limited labeled data and prolonged training times. A very common practice in deploying segmentation networks for tasks such as geospatial image analysis is a basic transfer learning approach, where the network is pretrained on another (presumably label-rich domain) and then fine-tuned with a limited amount of labeled data in the domain of interest. In this chapter, through experiments conducted on two benchmark geospatial datasets, we examine the factors impacting such a transfer learning performance with semantic segmentation models. Our findings reveal key observations and provide practical recommendations for leveraging such transfer learning for geospatial image analysis. © 2024 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
