AB  - In this paper, researchers propose an improved beam training and localization framework for Intelligent Reflecting Surfaces (IRS) based millimetre-wave (mmWave) communication. To choose the most effective beam direction that maximizes received signal power, the suggested system makes use of optimized beam selection, which is defined as (Formula presented.). Even in non-line-of-sight (NLOS) situations, the system enhances signal strength and sustains dependable communication through accurate IRS phase shift adjustment and user localization. In comparison to traditional methods, our simulations show that the optimized beam training algorithm yields a 22.7% reduction in localization error and a 15.3% improvement in communication rate. In restricted surroundings, the IRS-assisted system also exhibits a 30% improvement in signal-to-noise ratio (SNR). These outcomes demonstrate how well the suggested IRS-aided beam training approach works to improve location accuracy and communication efficiency for uses including autonomous systems, smart agriculture, and disaster response. © 2025 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.
