AB  - This research investigates the incorporation of GeoAI enabled spatial analysis to analyse long-term forest dynamic and ecological sensitivity in Goa India for regenerative tourism planning. Applying machine learning classification models to a high abstraction-quality 5-decade (1973-2022) or multi-temporal satellite time series analyse, we measure the conservative loss of forest cover by 3.75% with pronounced ecosystem fragmentation (e.g., an 200 km2 loss in old-growth extant forest). Using Ecological Sensitive Region (ESR) zoning framework for land cover mapping, 54% of Goa is assigned as highly sensitive (ESR-1 and ESR-2) that require conservation priority in the study area. These zones coincide with ecosystems of high biodiversity value and sequestering potential (56,131 Gg totaling 373 billion). Such analysis offers spatial strategies combining ecological preservation with local, low-impact tourism. By combining forest health variables with ESR mapping, this study yields a scalable, data-driven approach to help India meet its climate and tourist models based on restoration and sustainable. © 2025 IEEE.
