AB  - The proceedings contain 28 papers. The special focus in this conference is on FIG Commission. The topics include: Designing 3D Triangulated Irregular Network Data Structure for Surface and Subsurface Unified Spatial Data Model – Preliminary Work; Enhancing 3D Building Models Segmentation in CityGML; geospatial Analysis of Electric Vehicle Charging Infrastructure Deployment: Evaluation of Technical Factors via Artificial Intelligence; predictive Analysis of Road Accidents in Casablanca: A Machine Learning Approach; Development and Evaluation of Geo-AI for Healthcare Discovery; machine Learning for Semi-Automated Land Parcel Plotting; Assessing Height Determination Accuracy in Digital Terrain Models (DTM) Derived from UAV Data Using Sarawak Geocentric Datum; assessing the Impact and Efficiency of Cadastral Modernisation on Coordinate Systems for Orthophoto Production: A Comprehensive Evaluation for Town Planning; Projection of Sea Surface Salinity Using Ensemble of Selected CMIP6 GCMs of Bay-of-Bengal; Seasonal Variability of Sea Surface Salinity in Malaysian Waters Using Space-Based Observation of SMOS; investigation of Long-Term Sea Level Variation from Satellite Altimeter and Tide Gauge in Southeast Asia Region; a Review of Global Ocean Tide Models for Tidal Prediction to Support Hydrographic Separation Model; assessment of the Optimal Hydrodynamic Model for Malaysian Coastal Waters; Can Sentinel-1 SAR Deliver Accurate High-Resolution DEMs in Vegetated Humid Tropics?; Damage Assessment with YOLOv9 Instance Segmentation: An Analysis of the Marrakech Earthquake Case Study; satellite Based Assessment on the Water Yield Deficit at Sub-Watershed Level in Peninsular Malaysia During 2005 Drought; an Interactive Spatial Web-Based System for Exploring Sri Aman Tourism, Sarawak.
