AB  - The health risks associated with exposure to particulate matter (PM) and the complexities of monitoring air quality for large populations necessitate innovative solutions. Moreover, since individuals spend a significant portion of their time indoors, understanding indoor air quality becomes imperative. To address this, the present study proposes an integrated approach utilizing geospatial artificial intelligence (Geo-AI) methods to develop precise models for indoor PM (including PM10, PM2.5, and PM1) in indoor environment within residential households. © 2024 18th Conference of the International Society of Indoor Air Quality and Climate, INDOOR AIR 2024 - Conference Program and Proceedings. All rights reserved.
