AD  - St.Joseph's Institute of Technology, Artificial Intelligence and Data Science, Chennai, India
AB  - Disaster relief missions are usually hampered by disconnected communication, poor real-time awareness, and resource coordination inefficiencies. This paper introduces a Disaster Relief Resource Management Platform powered by AI and geospatial capabilities, developed with the MERN stack and Leaflet.js for map rendering. The platform provides five groundbreaking features: Geo-AI Prediction with Dynamic Heatmaps for detection of high-risk areas, a Digital Twin of affected areas for real-time simulation and tracking, a Multi-language and Voice-Enabled User Interface for accessibility support, Offline-first Architecture with Background Sync for seamless operation in network outage conditions, and a Unified Multi-Agency Dashboard for simplifying inter-agency coordination. Firebase is used for real-time data synchronization, and role-based dashboards aid in effective decision-making. The framework will enhance situational awareness, speed up response times, and provide inclusive disaster management, especially in low-connectivity or underserved areas.  © 2025 IEEE.
