AB  - This paper presents the development of a Digital Twin framework for establishing a unified cadastral reference system in Indonesia. The research addresses persistent issues in the national cadastre, including data gaps, overlaps, and inconsistencies across institutions that arise from fragmented survey campaigns, heterogeneous mapping standards, and the absence of a unified, three-dimensional cadastral reference system capable of reconciling multi-agency datasets. At the international level, most existing Digital Twin implementations focus on infrastructure, mobility, or generic 3D city models rather than legally binding cadastre, leaving a gap in national-scale cadastral digital twins particularly in developing-country contexts. Integrating Building Information Modelling (BIM), Geographic Information Systems (GIS), and Internet of Things (IoT) technologies, the proposed system provides a three-dimensional (3D) digital representation of land parcels, ownership, and related assets. Data acquisition was carried out using oblique photogrammetry with a UAV Trinity Pro equipped with a D2M oblique camera system, achieving geometric accuracy with CE90 of 0.047 m and LE90 of 0.822 m. The prototype system, visualized through a WebGIS platform using CesiumJS, demonstrates how Digital Twin technology can support interoperability and multipurpose cadastral management. The IoT layer is implemented by linking cadastral objects in the 3D model to fixed CCTV camera sensors and their live metadata streams, allowing users to contextualize real-time observations within the cadastral Digital Twin. The study establishes a foundation for future GeoAI-based analytics in cadastral automation, spatial anomaly detection, and predictive land management toward a fully intelligent national cadastral system. In particular, the proposed National Cadastral Digital Twin (NCDT) prototype demonstrates how oblique multi-view 3D data, BIM–CityGML semantics, and 3D Tiles web streaming can be operationalized into a legally compliant and interoperable cadastral reference framework tailored to Indonesia, providing a concrete proof-of-concept for an IoT-enabled cadastral Digital Twin aligned with the One Map Policy. © 2025 IEEE.
