AB  - This Research utilizes artificial intelligence and geospatial (Geo-AI) to optimize the efficiency of public transportation in West Jakarta, addressing traffic jam and urban mobility challenges. By integrating geospatial data and machine learning, this research analyzes the population density, road network, and public transportation stops. Data sourced from Portal Geo Spasial Indonesia, Badan Informasi Geospasial, and Open Street Map processed using QGIS and Python. The processing of the data focuses on administrative boundaries and the transportation infrastructures in West Jakarta. Data processing, spatial visualization, K-means clustering to cluster the district based on the population density and stop points of the transportation services. Analysis shows that the population distribution is not evenly distributed, with districts like Petamburan, Tambora, and Taman Sari showing high density, while others are less populated. Stop points data also shows that there are districts with an imbalance ratio of population density and the stop points. K-means Clustering, with Silhouette Score of 0.336 and an elbow point at K= 3 determined by the Elbow Method is used for the clustering process. Clustering results show districts with inadequate transportation services; this result could help in optimizing public transportation by increasing its efficiency and equalization of transportation services and access. Analysis results show that artificial intelligence and geospatial can be used to increase the user experience and optimize the services of public transportation. Future research could incorporate additional parameters and expand the scope to larger area; refining research methods could increase accuracy and the quality of result.  © 2025 IEEE.
