AB  - GeoAI (Geospatial Artificial Intelligence) is emerging as a core technology for intelligent national land management by addressing complex spatial challenges such as urbanization, environmental degradation, and disaster response. However, its practical adoption in Korea remains limited due to challenges in acquiring high-quality data, repetitive construction of training datasets, and insufficient technological maturity. This study aims to propose not only strategic directions for GeoAI advancement but also a concrete policy implementation framework. Based on literature review, megatrend analysis, expert surveys, and interviews, this research identifies key tasks such as establishing integrated spatial data infrastructure, developing location-encoded training datasets, and advancing foundation models and self-learning technologies. Furthermore, by outlining stakeholder-specific roles, phased implementation strategies, and institutional and financial linkages, the study enhances the practical applicability of GeoAI and provides a structured policy pathway for realizing intelligent land governance. © 2025, Korean Society of Surveying. All rights reserved.
