AB  - The study aims at GIS thematic map models and STATA graphs obtained from the daily increase in the various states of India. The KMeans Clustering is modeled to understand the clustering of each state nearby the other state. This helps to know that Covid-19 escalates from state to state based on the algorithm. During the pandemic period from 12 April 2020 through 23 May 2020, Covid-19 cases increased vigorously and reached a total of 125,101 reported cases in India. Four states are in the red zone Viz. Maharashtra (44582), Tamil Nadu (14753), Gujarat (13268), and Delhi (12319). This paper aims to study the Covid-19 using Geographic Information Systems models and Artificial Intelligence algorithms. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2023. All rights reserved.
