AB  - Benchmarking is widely used in the machine learning (ML) and AI community to facilitate competition between emerging methods. To do this, the methods must be trained using standard datasets and validated using standard performance metrics. This paper proposed a benchmark example labeling template: BM/challenge/GEOAI volume/year of publication. The example is thus labeled as BM/FootingDesign/1/2024. This paper further proposed a simple layout suitable for geo-related disciplines consisting of: (a) challenge statement, (b) physical problem, (c) site conditions, (d) geodata, (e) sample solution, and (f) performance metrics. This layout is illustrated using a data-driven site characterization challenge that leads to a quantifiable engineering impact in terms of a footing design. © 2025 The Authors. Published by Elsevier B.V. This is an open access article under the CC BY license. http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
