AB  - The proceedings contain 38 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Recent Advances in Artificial Intelligence and Smart Applications. The topics include: Designing an Audio CODEC with Synthesizing Generative Adversarial Networks; LOGIOUS: An Instant Messaging (IM) Platform Using AI; prediction of Groundwater Depth Using Average Rainfall-Groundwater Correlations in Kolkata, India; improved IoT Network Real-Time Anomaly Detection: A Machine Learning Approach to Boosting Security and Performance; Leaf Disease Detection Using YOLOv8; AI-Enabled Real-Time Next Generation Attendance Monitoring System with Facial Recognition; prediction of Gaze Point Using Deep Learning and Raspberry Pi; enhanced Deep Learning Model ResNet101 for Efficient Skin Disease Detection; an Email Spam Detection Approach Using Voting Ensemble Method; complex Power Quality Disturbance Classification Using Hilbert–Huang Transformation and Multiclass Support Vector Machine Classifier; character-Centric Summarization and Keyphrase Extraction with Visualization in Indian Mythology; Advanced Breast Cancer Diagnostics Through Comparative Analysis of Machine Learning Models by MRI Image Analysis; EdgeSwarm: Edge-Enabled Opportunistic UAV Network-Assisted Robotic Swarm for Post-Disaster Relief; Enhancing Student-Alumni Engagement Through a Graph-Driven Recommendation Framework with Paraphrase-MiniLM-L6-v2; enhancing Object Identification Using Deep Learning Algorithms for Assisting Disabled Individuals; eSmartView: An Embedded System for the Mobile Assistant to Recognize the Tumor and Virtually Identify the Affected Wing; machine Learning for the Present with Strategies for Real-Time Natural Disaster Response; The Frontier of Geospatial AI Deep Learning Applications in Data Mining and Spatial Analysis; deep Learning Insights into Meningeal Interleukin-17 T Cell’s Influence on Cognitive Dysfunction in Salt-Sensitive Hypertensive Mice; SMRITI—Semantic Model for Retrieval and Interpretation of