AB  - To implement data-based territorial policies, it is necessary to produce information from large volumes of data by applying data analysis and visualization, designing reasonable scenarios, computing and visualizing their impacts, and classifying them to help select the right actions to apply. To perform such activities, many issues need to be addressed. The aim of the present paper is to investigate the role of ICT within this process and recognize its main sectors that can contribute to provide expert users and decision makers with spatial knowledge useful to improve the exchange of strategic knowledge at the local level, produce innovation, and create cross-fertilization in terms of benefit for different domains. In addition to algorithms specifically conceived to manage data supply chain, different disciplines, ranging from Spatial Data Science to artificial intelligence, from IoT to location intelligence, are investigated to discuss how advances in some relevant key points can contribute to design a systemic approach to build networks and clusters of domains on which specific actions can be applied. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2022.
