AB  - The proceedings contain 32 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Geoinformatics in Sustainable Ecosystem and Society. The topics include: Spatialization Method of Atmospheric Quality Public Opinion Based on Natural Language Processing; Extension and Expression of OWL Modeling Primitives Based on Spatio-Temporal Ontology of Ocean Flow Field; research on Domain Ontology Modeling and Formal Expression of Ocean Flow Field; study on Space-Time Development of Urban Areas in Shenyang Using Landsat Remote Sensing Data; ecological Environment Evaluation of Liuxi River Basin During Rapid Urbanization; analysis of Urban Greenness Landscape and Its Spatial Association with Urbanization and Climate Changes; urban-Expansion Driven Farmland Loss Follows with the Environmental Kuznets Curve Hypothesis: Evidence from Temporal Analysis in Beijing, China; investigating Evolutions of Metro Station Functions in Shenzhen with Long-Term Smart Card Data; spatio-Temporal Evolution of Environmental Efficiency of Construction Land in Yangtze River Economic Zone; analysis of Potential Factors Influencing Ground-Level Ozone Concentrations in Chinese Cities; spectral Characteristics and Model Inversion of Common Greening Plants in Guangzhou Under Dust Pollution; analysis of Landscape Pattern Spatial Scale in Middle and Upper Reaches of Meijiang River Basin; Design of Distribution Network Pre-planning System Based on GIS; Validation and Comparison Among Different VIIRS Cloud Mask Products; a Semi-supervised Regression Method Based on Geography Weighted Regression Model; quality Evaluation of Sea Level Height Data of Jason-3 Satellite Based on Jason-2; evaluating Spatial Details of Luojia-1 Night-Time Images Using Road Network Analysis; preface; evaluation on Suitability of Oil and Gas Zoning in Nansha Sea.
