AB  - The proceedings contain 12 papers. The topics discussed include: sensing overlapping geospatial communities from human movements using graph affiliation generation models; towards the intelligent era of spatial analysis and modeling; incorporating spatial context for post-OCR in map images; highway2vec - representing OpenStreetMap microregions with respect to their road network characteristics; SHGCN: a hypergraph-based deep learning model for spatiotemporal traffic flow prediction; remote sensing visual question answering with a self-attention multi-modal encoder; IM2City: image geo-localization via multi-modal learning; real-time GeoAI for high-resolution mapping and segmentation of arctic permafrost features; density-based cluster detection at multiple spatial scales via Kullback-Leibler divergence of reachability profiles; unsupervised historical map registration by a deformation neural network; and fine-grained location prediction of non-geo-tagged tweets - a multi-view learning approach.
