AB  - Copernicus is the European Programme dedicated to achieving continuous, autonomous and high-quality capacity in Earth Observation. As part of the Emergency Management Service, the Exposure Mapping Component (Copernicus Global Human Settlement Layer) is tasked to provide global, reliable and up-to-date geospatial built-up surfaces and population information for operational crisis management. With the use of Earth observation data and advanced GeoAI technologies, the Global Human Settlement Layer is capable to deliver global 10 m built-up surface fraction maps, and residential/non-residential classification of built-up surfaces. The combination of built-up surface data with census data results in global population grids at 100 m resolution. This short paper reviews the key principles of the Copernicus Exposure Mapping component, the innovation the service is bringing, and the characteristics of the operational production for the years 2022, 2024, and 2026 it will produce as open and free data. © 2023 IEEE.
